# Atlas Fresh — Daily Export Planner
# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env (it is already in .gitignore).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The backend loads this file automatically at startup (python-dotenv), so
# `make run` is all you need. No export, no sourcing.
# Real environment variables still win over anything set here.
#
# With no variables set at all the app still runs: it reads the bundled
# workbook and the assistant falls back to the deterministic, engine-computed
# answers (no AI). That is the default and needs no paid service.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Input workbook
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Path to the .xlsx to read. Relative paths resolve from the repository root.
# Default: data/Atlas_Fresh_Production_Commercial_Data.xlsx
# The file is opened read only and is never modified.
ATLAS_DATA_PATH=data/Atlas_Fresh_Production_Commercial_Data.xlsx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Assistant (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The assistant only explains a plan the engine already computed. It never
# calculates, allocates or writes anything.
#
# It talks to any OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint, so OpenAI,
# Google Gemini and local gateways all work with the same three variables.

# Leave OPENAI_API_KEY empty to run with no AI. The UI then shows the
# deterministic summary and labels it as computed by the planning engine.
#
# --- Google Gemini: set these three, uncommented ---
#   Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
OPENAI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# --- Hosted OpenAI: replace the two lines above with these ---
#OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# --- Local gateway (Ollama, llama.cpp), no real key needed ---
#OPENAI_API_KEY=local
#OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#OPENAI_MODEL=llama3.1

# Notes
# - OPENAI_BASE_URL is the endpoint root. The app appends /chat/completions.
#   Leave it empty for hosted OpenAI (the built-in default).
# - OPENAI_MODEL defaults to gpt-4o-mini.
#   Gemini: gemini-3.8-flash (current), gemini-3.1-pro-preview
#   Local: llama3.1, qwen:7b, mistral
# - gemini-2.5-flash answers 404 "no longer available to new users". If a model
#   is retired, pick a current one from https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models
# - If the provider call fails, the app never breaks: it shows the
#   deterministic server-computed summary and says the live model was
#   unavailable, with the reason.
